  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="66">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northu">Northu</ref> 66</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="66" corresp="#wit-d">Gif ænig man heonan forð rihte laga wyrde, gebete hit georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">If anyone henceforth violates just laws, he is to compensate for it eagerly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin" corresp="#wit-d">Henceforth, if anyone violates just laws, he is to atone for it sincerely.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn jemand hinfort rechte Satzungen verletzt, büsse er es ernstlich.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone henceforth violates the right laws, let him atone for it earnestly.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Clauses 46 f. are repeated here, perhaps only through the confusion of the scribe, Liebermann thinks.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
